# Implementation Plan - Fix Broadcast Visibility in Chat

Broadcast messages are currently sent via the LINE API but are not recorded in the application's [Message](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx#16-23) database table. Consequently, they do not appear in the chat history.

To fix this, I will update the background worker to create a [Message](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx#16-23) record for each customer who successfully receives the broadcast.

## User Review Required

> [!NOTE]
> This change will strictly apply to **new** broadcasts. Old broadcasts that were already sent will not retrospectively appear in the chat history unless we run a migration (which is out of scope for this quick fix).

## Proposed Changes

### Background Worker

#### [MODIFY] [run.ts](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/workers/run.ts)
- Import `MessageType` and `Prisma` types.
- Inside the broadcasting loop, after successfully sending a message to LINE:
    - Create a [Message](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx#16-23) record in the database.
    - Set `type` to match the broadcast content (e.g., 'TEXT', 'IMAGE').
    - Set `direction` to `OUTBOUND`.
    - Set `status` to `SENT`.
    - Link it to the `broadcastId` and `customerId`.
    - Link it to the `conversationId` (fetch it from the customer relation).

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1.  Run the worker locally (`npx ts-node src/workers/run.ts` or ensure it's running).
2.  Send a new Broadcast from the Admin Panel.
3.  Wait for the broadcast to complete.
4.  Go to the Chat page for one of the recipients.
5.  Verify that the broadcast message appears in the chat history.
